// ApiKeyInvalidation — one credential that has stopped being valid.
//
// For a data-plane key both identifiers travel, because the receiver's caches
// are keyed differently: the authentication path by hash, the management read
// path by key id. Evicting one and not the other leaves a revoked key readable
// as enabled until its entry expires.
//
// For a management token only key_hash is meaningful, and it carries
// sha256(token) — the same value the store holds.
//
// No credential travels on this channel. Both fields are hashes or opaque
// identifiers, and a peer able to receive this message can already read the
